  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the delivery records for all four orders. Here's what I found and what I've done:\n\n**#6501, Saffron Lane (tonight):** It was due at 6:00 PM and handed to you at 6:52 PM, so 52 minutes late. For orders 45 or more minutes late, you get account credit of 20% of the subtotal. That comes to $25.60, but the maximum for Plus members is $25. **I've added $25.00 credit.**\n\n**#6502, Pho Real (Thursday):**\n- **Late delivery:** It was due at 7:15 PM and arrived at 7:45 PM, so 30 minutes late. Plus members get $5 for a delay this long. **I've added $5.00 credit.**\n- **Missing summer rolls:** Usually you could choose between a $9.00 refund to your card or $10.80 in credit. But there's a $40 limit on credit added in one conversation, and the two late credits already used $30, so I can't add $10.80 more. **I've refunded $9.00 to your Visa ending 4242.** It should show up in 3\u20135 business days.\n\n**#6503, Taqueria Luz (Tuesday):** We can't give compensation for this one. At 5:50 PM you got a push notification that the delivery time had changed to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. That notice came 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM time, so 7:00 PM became the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that. An order only counts as late if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the promised time.\n\n**#6504, Burger Barn (last Friday):** I'm sorry, but this one is past the deadline. It was about an hour late, but you can only claim for a late delivery within 7 days after it arrives. It arrived on Oct 16 at 8:00 PM, so the deadline was Oct 23 at 8:00 PM.\n\n**Summary:** You now have $30.00 in Forkful credit to use on future orders, and $9.00 is on its way back to your card.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for going through all four. I'm not thrilled about #6503 and #6504, but I'll take your word on the rules.\n\nOn the summer rolls, the refund to Visa is fine. I'd actually prefer the $10.80 as account credit, though. Could you check whether that's possible at all? If not, I'll take the $9.00 refund.\n\nAlso, before I go, can you confirm the $25 credit for #6501 and the $5 for #6502 are both on my account? I'd like to see them listed."
  },
